{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-knot-particle-generation","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:knot-particle-generation","kind":"definition","title":"Knot-particle generation from $T_{m,n}$ torus knot generators","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-skein-generation","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-color-tube-interpretation"],"tags":["knot","particle","generation","torus-knot","hopf-link","color-tube","skein","exceptional-divisor"],"defines":["torus-knot-generators"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Torsion.KnotParticleGeneration","text":"knot-particle-generation.md","leanSource":"knot-particle-generation.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:knot-particle-generation\"></a><p><em>The particle spectrum is generated from a finite set of torus knot generators <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,n}</code> (with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\gcd(m,n) = 1</code>) embedded in the standard torus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{T}^2 \\subset S^3</code>, together with two <a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-linking-operations\">linking operations</a> that act on the exceptional divisor and the color-tube fibration. The <dfn class=\"defterm\" id=\"term-torus-knot-generators\">torus knot generators</dfn> are the family</em></p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  \\mathcal{G} =  \\bigl\\{ T_{m,n}  \\big| \n  \\gcd(m,n) = 1, m &#x3C; n,\n  m + n \\leq N(\\chi) \\bigr\\},</code></pre>\n<p><em>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T_{m,n}</code> winds <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">m</code> times around the meridian and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n</code> times around the longitude of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{T}^2</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N(\\chi)</code> is a cutoff determined by the Euler characteristic of the Frobenius--Hopf object.</em> For the Descartes universe with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\chi_{\\mathrm{eu}}(M_0) = -6</code>, the bound is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N(-6) = 9</code>, admitting:</p>\n<p>See <a href=\"#tbl:knot-particle-generation-table-data\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/skein-particle-generation\">Table</a>.</p>\n<p>One reserves <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> for the substrate parameter and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p</code> for base points. The winding indices are always <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(m,n)</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/knot-particle-generation.md","heading":"Definition","number":"9.4.2","page":"b/def-knot-particle-generation","qa":{"counts":{"pass":75,"fail":2,"warn":4,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.LiftingDescent.KnotParticleGeneration","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/knot-particle-generation.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
